From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ridertan02-collab <ridertan02-collab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:53:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] host/ios: a screen wider than 16:9 takes its own picture
 shape

DM_SCREEN_ASPECT now works in the wide direction (1.3 to 2.4): a wide
shape keeps the output 1920 wide and takes the height 1920 / ratio as a
multiple of 8 (2.17 -> 1920x880; the 48 grid left the picture 2.2 % off
such a screen and the present cropped), the layout height stays 2/3 of
it rounded, and a scene of the screen's ratio keeps the 16:9 vertical
angle (k floored at 1: the sides widen instead of the view narrowing).
The iOS front end's picture shape auto resolves a lying phone's window
(19.5:9) instead of falling back to 16:9, and the launcher's Picture
shape row offers 2.17 (iPhone screen, 19.5:9).

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: this fork's product goal: games fill a 19.5:9 phone panel edge to edge; upstream #2609/#2891/#3042 carry the same direction
Issue: fork-wide-aspect bring-up (see patches/README.md)

